# Kernel tuning workspace: untracked by default, with the correctness gate
# explicitly allowed back in.
#
# Excluded for two reasons:
#   * oracle/*.pt is 44 GB (flash_T32_fp32.pt alone is 12 GB -- it holds all 256
#     experts' weights). Regenerable, see below.
#   * report.html / plan.md / draft.md / benchmark*.csv / duipai_*.csv /
#     profile.ncu-rep are tuning residue. The ncu-rep is also a binary tied to the
#     GPU it was captured on (SM 12.0 here), so it means nothing elsewhere.
#
# Allowed back in because the production kernels (kernels/*.py) do not import
# workspace -- it is not a runtime dependency -- but it is the entire basis of the
# kernel's VERIFIABILITY. Without duipai.py + build_oracle.py +
# oracle/manifest.jsonl, moe_dispatch_fused.py becomes a kernel you can only
# trust, never check; and it is not an ordinary optimisation (fused MoE moved
# alpha from 0.761 to 0.556, because draft and target each flip tokens
# independently). CONTRACT.md pins the training/inference mode and is required
# reading before touching the kernel.
#
# Rebuilding the oracle, from the repo root:
#     python kernels/workspace/<kernel>/build_oracle.py
# manifest.jsonl records each fixture's T/k/E/H/I/dtype/scale/concentration.
kernels/workspace/**
# Directories must be allowed back first, or git never descends into them and
# every ! below is dead.
!kernels/workspace/**/
!kernels/workspace/__init__.py
!kernels/workspace/*/__init__.py
!kernels/workspace/*/CONTRACT.md
!kernels/workspace/*/build_oracle.py
!kernels/workspace/*/duipai.py
!kernels/workspace/*/verify_model.py
!kernels/workspace/*/oracle/manifest.jsonl

# Local-only.
#   docs/     result write-ups and the HTML tables (rolling intermediate findings)
#   models/   local checkpoint copies (SDAR-1_7B-Chat etc., fetched from HF)
#   scripts/  orchestration and sweep drivers
# run_protocol.py and configs/protocol/*.yaml are NOT here -- they are the entry
# point and the single source of truth for the calibrated settings, so both are
# tracked. scripts/env.sh is inlined into run_protocol.py's ENV_DEFAULTS, so the
# entry point does not depend on scripts/.
docs/
models/
scripts/
